{"title":"SCC Generated CKLB at: 2026-09-05T10:13:28","id":"948300D4-6BF8-1014-BBAE-F1AFA960E9F7","target_data":{"target_type":"Computing","mac_address":"00:0C:29:61:C8:22","role":"Workstation","fqdn":"WKS5-SOTERIA.","host_name":"WKS5-SOTERIA","ip_address":"192.168.40.95"},"stigs":[{"size":67,"version":"2","rules":[{"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; \"Configure detection for potentially unwanted applications\" is set to \"Enabled\" and \"Block\".\n\nUse the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \n\nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\n\nIf the value \"PUAProtection\" does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nIf the value \"PUAProtection\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.","ccis":["CCI-001243"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-213426","title":"SRG-APP-000279"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Configure detection for potentially unwanted applications is set to 'Enabled' and 'Block')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:1000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Configure detection for potentially unwanted applications is set to 'Enabled' and 'Block'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:1000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Configure detection for potentially unwanted applications registry setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PUAProtection'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:1000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Is the registry setting a red_dword set to 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender'\n                        : name equals 'PUAProtection'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:1","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213426","false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; \"Configure Detection for Potentially Unwanted Applications\" to \"Enabled\" and \"Block\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to block the Potentially Unwanted Application (PUA) feature.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"responsibility":"","uuid":"947AE2B5-6BF8-1014-9C0D-D6D431779220","group_title":"SRG-APP-000279","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213426r961197","legacy_ids":["SV-89827","V-75147"],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"After enabling this feature, PUA protection blocking takes effect on endpoint clients after the next signature update or computer restart. Signature updates take place daily under typical circumstances. PUA will be blocked and automatically quarantined.","group_id_src":"V-213426","severity":"high","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213426r961197_rule","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000001","ia_controls":""},{"false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; \"Turn off routine remediation\" to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to automatically take action on all detected tasks.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001243"],"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; \"Turn off routine remediation\" is set to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableRoutinelyTakingAction\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1, this is a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000279","id":"V-213427"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Turn off routine remediation)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:2000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Turn off routine remediation\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:2000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Turn off routine remediation\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableRoutinelyTakingAction'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:2000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Turn off routine remediation\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:2","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213427","legacy_ids":["SV-89831","V-75151"],"mitigations":"","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","discussion":"This policy setting allows Microsoft Defender configuration to automatically take action on all detected threats. The action to be taken on a particular threat is determined by the combination of the policy-defined action user-defined action and the signature-defined action. If this policy setting is enabled, Microsoft Defender does not automatically take action on the detected threats but prompts users to choose from the actions available for each threat. If this policy setting is disabled or not configured, Microsoft Defender automatically takes action on all detected threats after a nonconfigurable delay of approximately five seconds.","group_id_src":"V-213427","severity":"medium","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","rule_id_src":"SV-213427r961197_rule","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000003","responsibility":"","uuid":"947AF511-6BF8-1014-8EF6-E967A92CB8DE","group_title":"SRG-APP-000279","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213427r961197"},{"weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213428r1190706","uuid":"947B02DE-6BF8-1014-B5ED-8FD4CABEEA8E","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000004","rule_id_src":"SV-213428r1190706_rule","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting turns off Microsoft Defender Antivirus. If this policy setting is enabled, Microsoft Defender Antivirus does not run and computers are not scanned for malware or other potentially unwanted software. \n\nWhen the setting is disabled and a third-party antivirus solution is installed, the two applications can both simultaneously try to protect the system. The two AV solutions both attempt to quarantine the same threat and will fight for access to delete the file. Users will see conflicts and the system may lock up until the two solutions finish processing. \n\nWhen the setting is not configured and a third-party antivirus solution is installed, both applications coexist on the system without conflicts. Defender Antivirus will automatically disable itself and will enable if the third-party solution stops functioning. When the setting is not configured and Defender Antivirus is the only AV solution, Defender AV will run (default state) and receive definition updates. An administrator account is needed to turn off the service. A standard user cannot disable the service.","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89833","V-75153"],"security_override_guidance":"","severity":"high","group_id_src":"V-213428","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:3"},"group_id":"V-213428","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Micrsoft Defender Antivirus\\Turn off Windows Defender Antivirus)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:3000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Micrsoft Defender Antivirus\\Turn off Windows Defender Antivirus\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:3000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Turn off Windows Defender Antivirus\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableAntiSpyware'\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-213428","title":"SRG-APP-000278"},"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; \"Turn off Windows Defender Antivirus\" is set to âNot Configuredâ.\n\nFor Windows 10:\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableAntiSpyware\" does not exist, this is not a finding.","ccis":["CCI-002624"],"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to run and scan for malware and other potentially unwanted software.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"For Windows 10: Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus \"Turn off Microsoft Defender Antivirus\" to \"Not Configured\". \n","documentable":"false"},{"comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to not exclude files for scanning.","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Exclusions &gt;&gt; \"Path Exclusions\" to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","third_party_tools":"","false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Exclusions\\Path Exclusions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:4000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Exclusions\\Path Exclusions\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:4000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Exclusions\\Path Exclusions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Exclusions'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Exclusions_Paths'\n","group_id":"V-213429","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:4"},"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Exclusions &gt;&gt; \"Path Exclusions\" is set to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured.\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Exclusions\n \nCriteria: If the value \"Exclusions_Paths\" does not exist, this is not a finding.","ccis":["CCI-002624"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-213429","title":"SRG-APP-000278"},"rule_id_src":"SV-213429r1190707_rule","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000005","ia_controls":"","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213429","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89835","V-75155"],"reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","discussion":"This policy setting allows disabling of scheduled and real-time scanning for files under the paths specified or for the fully qualified resources specified. Paths should be added under the Options for this setting. Each entry must be listed as a name value pair where the name should be a string representation of a path or a fully qualified resource name. As an example, a path might be defined as: \"c:\\Windows\" to exclude all files in this directory. A fully qualified resource name might be defined as: \"C:\\Windows\\App.exe\". The value is not used and it is recommended that this be set to 0.\n\nExceptions can be made to allow file/folders that are impacting enterprise applications to be excluded from being scanned. All exclusions should be documented and approved.","rule_id":"SV-213429r1190707","weight":"10.0","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","responsibility":"","uuid":"947B0BFD-6BF8-1014-B7A4-A4414F7C2501"},{"third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Exclusions &gt;&gt; \"Process Exclusions\" to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","documentable":"false","status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","comments":null,"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to not exclude files opened by specified processes.","mitigation_control":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000278","id":"V-213430"},"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Exclusions &gt;&gt; \"Process Exclusions\" is set to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Exclusions\n\nCriteria: If the value \"Exclusions_Processes\" does not exist, this is not a finding.","ccis":["CCI-002624"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:5"},"group_id":"V-213430","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Exclusions\\Process Exclusions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:5000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Exclusions\\Process Exclusions\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:5000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Exclusions\\Process Exclusions\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Exclusions'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Exclusions_Processes'\n","security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213430","discussion":"This policy setting allows the disabling of scheduled and real-time scanning for any file opened by any of the specified processes. The process itself will not be excluded. To exclude the process, use the Path exclusion. Processes should be added under the options for this setting. Each entry must be listed as a name value pair where the name should be a string representation of the path to the process image. Note that only executables can be excluded. For example, a process might be defined as: \"c:\\windows\\app.exe\". The value is not used and it is recommended that this be set to 0.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-89837","V-75157"],"mitigations":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000006","rule_id_src":"SV-213430r1190710_rule","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","uuid":"947B1447-6BF8-1014-AD9D-968806B9827F","responsibility":"","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213430r1190710"},{"responsibility":"","uuid":"947B1C53-6BF8-1014-BD84-BCCF1D497D74","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213431r1190712","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89839","V-75159"],"discussion":"This setting allows an administrator to specify if Automatic Exclusions feature for Server SKUs should be turned off.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","group_id_src":"V-213431","severity":"medium","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","rule_id_src":"SV-213431r1190712_rule","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000007","check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Exclusions &gt;&gt; \"Turn off Auto Exclusions\" is set to \"Disabled\".\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Exclusions\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableAutoExclusions\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","ccis":["CCI-002624"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-213431","title":"SRG-APP-000278"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Exclusions\\Turn off Auto Exclusions)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:6000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Exclusions\\Turn off Auto Exclusions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:6000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Exclusions'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'DisableAutoExclusions'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Exclusions'\n                        : name equals 'DisableAutoExclusions'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134331004360000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_id":"V-213431","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:6"},"false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Exclusions &gt;&gt; \"Turn off Auto Exclusions\" to \"Disabled\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to enable the Automatic Exclusions feature.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null},{"responsibility":"","uuid":"947B23D5-6BF8-1014-8EC6-FB7CE7285A45","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","rule_id":"SV-213432r961092","weight":"10.0","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89841","V-75161"],"reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","discussion":"This policy setting configures a local override for the configuration to join Microsoft MAPS. This setting can only be set by Group Policy. If this setting is enabled, the local preference setting will take priority over Group Policy. If this setting is disabled or not configured, Group Policy will take priority over the local preference setting.","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213432","security_override_guidance":"","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","rule_id_src":"SV-213432r961092_rule","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000008","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"check_content":"This is applicable to unclassified systems. For other systems this is NA.\n\nVerify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; MAPS &gt;&gt; \"Configure local setting override for reporting to Microsoft MAPS\" is set to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n     \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet\n\nCriteria: If the value \"LocalSettingOverrideSpynetReporting\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1, this is a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-213432","title":"SRG-APP-000210"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Configure local setting override for reporting to Microsoft MAPS)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:7000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Configure local setting override for reporting to Microsoft MAPS\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:7000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Configure local setting override for reporting to Microsoft MAPS\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LocalSettingOverrideSpynetReporting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:7000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Configure local setting override for reporting to Microsoft MAPS\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:7"},"group_id":"V-213432","false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","documentable":"false","fix_text":"This is applicable to unclassified systems. For other systems this is NA.\n\nSet the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; MAPS &gt;&gt; \"Configure local setting override for reporting to Microsoft MAPS\" to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to disable local setting override for reporting to Microsoft MAPS.","comments":null},{"group_id":"V-213433","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:8"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Configure the Block at First Sight)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet\\DisableBlockAtFirstSeen'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:8000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Configure the Block at First Sight\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:8000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Configure the Block at First Sight\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableBlockAtFirstSeen'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:8000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Configure the Block at First Sight\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet\\DisableBlockAtFirstSeen'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-213433","title":"SRG-APP-000278"},"check_content":"This is applicable to unclassified systems. For other systems this is NA.\n\nVerify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; MAPS &gt;&gt; \"Configure the 'Block at First Sight' feature\" is set to \"Enabled\".\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableBlockAtFirstSeen\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","ccis":["CCI-002624"],"comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to check in real time with MAPS before content is run or accessed.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"This is applicable to unclassified systems. For other systems this is NA.\n\nSet the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; MAPS &gt;&gt; \"Configure the 'Block at First Sight' feature\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"open","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-213433r1190715","weight":"10.0","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","uuid":"947B2FEA-6BF8-1014-94CA-F7B6D11100F0","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000009","rule_id_src":"SV-213433r1190715_rule","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213433","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This feature ensures the device checks in real time with the Microsoft Active Protection Service (MAPS) before allowing certain content to be run or accessed. If this feature is disabled, the check will not occur, which will lower the protection state of the device. \n\nEnabled - The Block at First Sight setting is turned on. \nDisabled - The Block at First Sight setting is turned off. \n\nThis feature requires these Group Policy settings to be set as follows: \nMAPS &gt;&gt; The \"Join Microsoft MAPS\" must be enabled or the \"Block at First Sight\" feature will not function. \nMAPS &gt;&gt; The \"Send file samples when further analysis is required\" should be set to 1 (Send safe samples) or 3 (Send all samples). Setting to 0 (Always Prompt) will lower the protection state of the device. Setting to 2 (Never send) means the \"Block at First Sight\" feature will not function. \nReal-time Protection &gt;&gt; The \"Scan all downloaded files and attachments\" policy must be enabled or the \"Block at First Sight\" feature will not function. \nReal-time Protection &gt;&gt; Do not enable the \"Turn off real-time protection\" policy or the \"Block at First Sight\" feature will not function.","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-89843","V-75163"],"mitigations":""},{"status":"open","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"This is applicable to unclassified systems. For other systems this is Not Applicable.\n\nSet the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; MAPS &gt;&gt; \"Join Microsoft MAPS\" to \"Enabled\" and select \"Basic MAPS\" or \"Advanced MAPS\" from the drop-down box.","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must join Microsoft MAPS.","comments":null,"group_tree":{"id":"V-213434","title":"SRG-APP-000210"},"ccis":["CCI-001170"],"check_content":"This is applicable to unclassified systems. For other systems, this is Not Applicable.\n\nVerify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; MAPS &gt;&gt; \"Join Microsoft MAPS\" is set to \"Enabled\" and \"Advanced MAPS\" is selected from the drop-down box.\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet\n\nCriteria: If the value \"SpynetReporting\" is REG_DWORD = 1, or REG_DWORD = 2, this is not a finding.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windowsdefav:def:213434","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213434","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (SpynetReporting == 1 or 2)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet\\SpynetReporting'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:21343400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : SpynetReporting == 1 or 2\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:21343400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SpynetReporting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet\\SpynetReporting'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting allows joining Microsoft MAPS. Microsoft MAPS is the online community that helps in choosing how to respond to potential threats. The community also helps stop the spread of new malicious software infections. You can choose to send basic or additional information about detected software. Additional information helps Microsoft create new definitions and protect your computer. This information can include things like location of detected items on your computer if harmful software was removed. The information will be automatically collected and sent. In some instances personal information might unintentionally be sent to Microsoft. However Microsoft will not use this information to identify you or contact you. \n\nPossible options are: \n(0x0) Disabled (default) \n(0x1) Basic membership \n(0x2) Advanced membership \n\nBasic membership will send basic information to Microsoft about software that has been detected, including where the software came from, the actions that you apply or that are applied automatically, and whether the actions were successful. Advanced membership will send, in addition to basic information, more information to Microsoft about malicious software spyware and potentially unwanted software, including the location of the software file names, how the software operates, and how it has impacted your computer. \n\nIf this setting is enabled, you will join Microsoft MAPS with the membership specified. If this setting is disabled or do not configured, you will not join Microsoft MAPS. In Windows 10, Basic membership is no longer available, so setting the value to 1 or 2 enrolls the device into Advanced membership.","legacy_ids":["SV-89847","V-75167"],"mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213434","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000010","rule_id_src":"SV-213434r1134051_rule","uuid":"947B3B65-6BF8-1014-9F52-8B95EA3FB825","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","rule_id":"SV-213434r1134051","weight":"10.0"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Send file samples when further analysis is required)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet\\SubmitSamplesConsent'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:10000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Send file samples when further analysis is required\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:10000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Send file samples when further analysis is required\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SubmitSamplesConsent'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:10000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\MAPS\\Send file samples when further analysis is required\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet\\SubmitSamplesConsent'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","group_id":"V-213435","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:10","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"check_content":"This is applicable to unclassified systems. For other systems this is NA.\n\nVerify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; MAPS &gt;&gt; \"Send file samples when further analysis is required\" is set to \"Enabled\" and \"Send safe samples\" is selected from the drop-down box.\n     \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Spynet\n\nCriteria: If the value \"SubmitSamplesConsent\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"group_tree":{"id":"V-213435","title":"SRG-APP-000210"},"mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to only send safe samples for MAPS telemetry.","comments":null,"false_positives":"","status":"open","documentable":"false","fix_text":"This is applicable to unclassified systems. For other systems this is NA.\n\nSet the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; MAPS &gt;&gt; \"Send file samples when further analysis is required\" to \"Enabled\" and select \"Send safe samples\" from the drop-down box.","third_party_tools":"","rule_id":"SV-213435r961092","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","uuid":"947B45E9-6BF8-1014-8C31-861C8A9850B7","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213435r961092_rule","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000011","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89887","V-75207"],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting configures behavior of samples submission when opt-in for MAPS telemetry is set. Possible options are:  \n(0x0) Always prompt\n(0x1) Send safe samples automatically \n(0x2) Never send  \n(0x3) Send all samples automatically","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213435","security_override_guidance":""},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:11","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213436","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Network Inspection System\\Turn on protocol recognition)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:11000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Network Inspection System\\Turn on protocol recognition\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:11000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\NIS'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableProtocolRecognition'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:11000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-213436","title":"SRG-APP-000278"},"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Network Inspection System &gt;&gt; \"Turn on protocol recognition\" is set to \"Enabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key:\nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\NIS\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableProtocolRecognition\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1, this is a finding.","ccis":["CCI-002624"],"comments":null,"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured for protocol recognition for network protection.","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Network Inspection System &gt;&gt; \"Turn on protocol recognition\" to \"Enabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","documentable":"false","status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213436r1190716","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","uuid":"947B4F79-6BF8-1014-B99D-C5DA2231B5F8","responsibility":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000012","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213436r1190716_rule","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213436","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting allows the configuration of protocol recognition for network protection against exploits of known vulnerabilities. If this setting is enabled or not configured, protocol recognition will be enabled. If this setting is disabled, protocol recognition will be disabled.","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89889","V-75209"]},{"potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000013","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213437r960921_rule","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting configures a local override for the configuration of monitoring for file and program activity on your computer. This setting can only be set by Group Policy. If this setting is enabled, the local preference setting will take priority over Group Policy. If this setting is disabled or not configured, Group Policy will take priority over the local preference setting.","legacy_ids":["SV-89891","V-75211"],"mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","group_id_src":"V-213437","severity":"medium","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213437r960921","uuid":"947B5955-6BF8-1014-88EF-EC3CB0B0760C","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000112","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to not allow local override of monitoring for file and program activity.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Configure local setting override for monitoring file and program activity on your computer\" to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","documentable":"false","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:12"},"group_id":"V-213437","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Microsoft Defender Antivirus/Real-time Protection/Configure local setting override for monitoring file and program activity on your computer is set to Disabled or Not Configured)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:12000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Microsoft Defender Antivirus/Real-time Protection/Configure local setting override for monitoring file and program activity on your computer is set to Disabled or Not Configured\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:12000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObje