all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n"},{"discussion":"This policy setting configures a local override for the configuration to turn on real-time protection. This setting can only be set by Group Policy. If this setting is enabled, the local preference setting will take priority over Group Policy. If this setting is disabled or not configured, Group Policy will take priority over the local preference setting.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-89899","V-75219"],"mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213441","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000017","rule_id_src":"SV-213441r1190717_rule","uuid":"947B8250-6BF8-1014-91C9-D054FEDDBC30","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213441r1190717","status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Configure local setting override to turn on real-time protection\" to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","documentable":"false","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV Group Policy settings must take priority over the local preference settings.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000278","id":"V-213441"},"ccis":["CCI-002624"],"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Configure local setting override to turn on real-time protection\" is set to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection\n\nCriteria: If the value \"LocalSettingOverrideDisableRealtimeMonitoring\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1, this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:16","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213441","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Configure local setting override to turn on real-time protection)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:16000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Configure local setting override to turn on real-time protection\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:16000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Configure local setting override to turn on real-time protection\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LocalSettingOverrideDisableRealtimeMonitoring'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:16000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Configure local setting override to turn on real-time protection\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n"},{"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must monitor for incoming and outgoing files.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Configure monitoring for incoming and outgoing file and program activity\" to \"Enabled\" with a policy option value of \"bi-directional (full on-access)\".","documentable":"false","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:17"},"group_id":"V-213442","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Configure monitoring for incoming and outgoing file and program activity)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:17000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Configure monitoring for incoming and outgoing file and program activity\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:17000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Configure monitoring for incoming and outgoing file and program activity\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RealtimeScanDirection'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:17000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Configure monitoring for incoming and outgoing file and program activity\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000278","id":"V-213442"},"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Configure monitoring for incoming and outgoing file and program activity\" is set to \"Enabled\" with a policy option value of \"bi-directional (full on-access)\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection\n\nCriteria: If the value \"RealtimeScanDirection\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1 or 2, this is a finding.","ccis":["CCI-002624"],"potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000018","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213442r1190718_rule","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","discussion":"This policy setting allows the configuration of monitoring for incoming and outgoing files without having to turn off monitoring entirely. It is recommended for use on servers that have a lot of incoming and outgoing file activity but for performance reasons need to have scanning disabled for a particular scan direction. The appropriate configuration should be evaluated based on the server role. Note that this configuration is only honored for NTFS volumes. For any other file system type, full monitoring of file and program activity will be present on those volumes. \n\nThe options for this setting are mutually exclusive: \n0 = Scan incoming and outgoing files (default) \n1 = Scan incoming files only \n2 = Scan outgoing files only \n\nAny other value, or if the value does not exist, resolves to the default (0). If this setting is enabled, the specified type of monitoring will be enabled. If this setting is disabled or not configured, monitoring for incoming and outgoing files will be enabled.","legacy_ids":["SV-89901","V-75221"],"mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","group_id_src":"V-213442","severity":"medium","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213442r1190718","uuid":"947B8B7A-6BF8-1014-AC56-8478CCD30EF6","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278"},{"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000278","id":"V-213443"},"ccis":["CCI-002624"],"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Monitor file and program activity on your computer to be scanned\" is set to \"Enabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableOnAccessProtection\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1, this is a finding.","group_id":"V-213443","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:18"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true ('Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Monitor file and program activity on your computer' is set to 'Enabled' or 'Not Configured')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:18000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Monitor file and program activity on your computer' is set to 'Enabled' or 'Not Configured'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:18000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : The corresponding registry entry for 'Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Monitor file and program activity on your computer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableOnAccessProtection'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:18000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : The expected reg_dword value for 'Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Monitor file and program activity on your computer'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Monitor file and program activity on your computer\" to \"Enabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","documentable":"false","status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","comments":null,"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to monitor for file and program activity.","mitigation_control":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","uuid":"947B9809-6BF8-1014-A3A3-DE9074789617","responsibility":"","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213443r1190719","security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213443","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting allows configuration of monitoring for file and program activity. If this setting is enabled or not configured, monitoring for file and program activity will be enabled. If this setting is disabled, monitoring for file and program activity will be disabled.","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89903","V-75223"],"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000019","rule_id_src":"SV-213443r1190719_rule","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C"},{"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:19"},"group_id":"V-213444","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Scan all downloaded files and attachments)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:19000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Scan all downloaded files and attachments\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:19000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Scan all downloaded files and attachments\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableIOAVProtection'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:19000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Scan all downloaded files and attachments\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-213444","title":"SRG-APP-000209"},"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Scan all downloaded files and attachments\" is set to \"Enabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableIOAVProtection\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1, this is a finding.","ccis":["CCI-001169"],"comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to scan all downloaded files and attachments.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Scan all downloaded files and attachments\" to \"Enabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-213444r961089","weight":"10.0","group_title":"SRG-APP-000209","uuid":"947B9F87-6BF8-1014-984F-B1E32AABE309","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000020","rule_id_src":"SV-213444r961089_rule","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213444","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","discussion":"This policy setting allows configuration of scanning for all downloaded files and attachments. If this setting is enabled or not configured, scanning for all downloaded files and attachments will be enabled. If this setting is disabled, scanning for all downloaded files and attachments will be disabled.","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89905","V-75225"]},{"rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000021","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213445r1190720_rule","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","security_override_guidance":"","group_id_src":"V-213445","severity":"medium","discussion":"This policy setting turns off real-time protection prompts for known malware detection. Microsoft Defender Antivirus alerts when malware or potentially unwanted software attempts to install itself or to run on a user's computer. If this policy setting is enabled, Microsoft Defender Antivirus will not prompt users to take actions on malware detections. If this policy setting is disabled or not configured, Microsoft Defender Antivirus will prompt users to take actions on malware detections.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89907","V-75227"],"rule_id":"SV-213445r1190720","weight":"10.0","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","uuid":"947BA6D9-6BF8-1014-9C48-85EEA607EA72","responsibility":"","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to always enable real-time protection.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Turn off real-time protection\" to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:20"},"group_id":"V-213445","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResu