dows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Turn off real-time protection\" is set to \"Disabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableRealtimeMonitoring\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1, this is a finding.","ccis":["CCI-002624"]},{"potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","rule_id_src":"SV-213446r961092_rule","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000022","ia_controls":"","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89909","V-75229"],"reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting allows configuration of behavior monitoring. If this setting is enabled or not configured, behavior monitoring will be enabled. If this setting is disabled, behavior monitoring will be disabled.","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213446","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id":"SV-213446r961092","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","uuid":"947BAE32-6BF8-1014-9551-FD965D1C3818","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to enable behavior monitoring.","comments":null,"false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Turn on behavior monitoring\" to \"Enabled \" or \"Not Configured\".","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Turn on behavior monitoring)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:21000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Turn on behavior monitoring\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:21000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Turn on behavior monitoring\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableBehaviorMonitoring'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:21000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Turn on behavior monitoring\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:21","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213446","check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Turn on behavior monitoring\" is set to \"Enabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableBehaviorMonitoring\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1, this is a finding.","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000210","id":"V-213446"}},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Turn on process scanning whenever real-time protection is enabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:22000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Turn on process scanning whenever real-time protection is enabled\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:22000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Turn on process scanning whenever real-time protection is enabled\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableScanOnRealtimeEnable'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:22000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Real-time Protection\\Turn on process scanning whenever real-time protection is enabled\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:22","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213447","ccis":["CCI-002624"],"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Turn on process scanning whenever real-time protection is enabled\" is set to \"Enabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Real-Time Protection\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableScanOnRealtimeEnable\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1, this is a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000278","id":"V-213447"},"comments":null,"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to process scanning when real-time protection is enabled.","mitigation_control":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Real-time Protection &gt;&gt; \"Turn on process scanning whenever real-time protection is enabled\" to \"Enabled\" or \"Not Configured\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213447r1190721","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","responsibility":"","uuid":"947BB957-6BF8-1014-9A85-95488C09B76F","rule_id_src":"SV-213447r1190721_rule","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000023","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","group_id_src":"V-213447","severity":"medium","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89911","V-75231"],"mitigations":"","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting allows the configuration of process scanning when real-time protection is turned on. This helps to catch malware, which could start when real-time protection is turned off. If this setting is enabled or not configured, a process scan will be initiated when real-time protection is turned on. If this setting is disabled, a process scan will not be initiated when real-time protection is turned on."},{"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to scan archive files.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Scan &gt;&gt; \"Scan archive files\" to \"Enabled \" or \"Not Configured\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Scan archive files)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:23000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Scan archive files\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:23000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Scan archive files\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableArchiveScanning'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:23000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Scan archive files\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:23"},"group_id":"V-213448","ccis":["CCI-002624"],"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Scan &gt;&gt; \"Scan archive files\" is set to \"Enabled\" or \"Not Configured\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableArchiveScanning\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value does not exist, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 1, this is a finding.","group_tree":{"id":"V-213448","title":"SRG-APP-000278"},"potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","rule_id_src":"SV-213448r1190722_rule","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000024","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89913","V-75233"],"reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","discussion":"This policy setting allows the configuration of scans for malicious software and unwanted software in archive files such as .ZIP or .CAB files. If this setting is enabled or not configured, archive files will be scanned. If this setting is disabled, archive files will not be scanned.","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213448","security_override_guidance":"","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213448r1190722","responsibility":"","uuid":"947BC140-6BF8-1014-BC70-E297059682B2","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278"},{"group_id":"V-213449","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:24","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Scan removable drives)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:24000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Scan removable drives\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:24000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Scan removable drives\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableRemovableDriveScanning'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:24000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Scan removable drives\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan'\n                        : name equals 'DisableRemovableDriveScanning'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-213449","title":"SRG-APP-000073"},"ccis":["CCI-000870"],"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Scan &gt;&gt; \"Scan removable drives\" is set to \"Enabled\".\n \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableRemovableDriveScanning\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to scan removable drives.","comments":null,"status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Scan &gt;&gt; \"Scan removable drives\" to \"Enabled\".","rule_id":"SV-213449r960852","weight":"10.0","uuid":"947BC8AC-6BF8-1014-BACD-C93C84505796","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000073","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000025","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213449r960852_rule","discussion":"This policy setting allows the management of whether or not to scan for malicious software and unwanted software in the contents of removable drives such as USB flash drives when running a full scan. If this setting is enabled, removable drives will be scanned during any type of scan. If this setting is disabled or not configured, removable drives will not be scanned during a full scan. Removable drives may still be scanned during quick scan and custom scan.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-89915","V-75235"],"mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213449"},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:25","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213450","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Specify the day of the week to run a scheduled scan)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:25000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Specify the day of the week to run a scheduled scan\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:25000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Specify the day of the week to run a scheduled scan\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ScheduleDay'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:25000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Scan\\Specify the day of the week to run a scheduled scan\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '7'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan'\n                        : name equals 'ScheduleDay'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-213450","title":"SRG-APP-000277"},"ccis":["CCI-001241"],"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Scan &gt;&gt; \"Specify the day of the week to run a scheduled scan\" is set to \"Enabled\" and anything other than \"Never\" is selected in the drop-down box.\n  \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan\n\nCriteria: If the value \"ScheduleDay\" is REG_DWORD = 0x8, this is a finding.\n\nValues of 0x0 through 0x7 are acceptable and not a finding.","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to perform a weekly scheduled scan.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Scan &gt;&gt; \"Specify the day of the week to run a scheduled scan\" to \"Enabled \" and select anything other than \"Never\" in the drop-down box.","status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-213450r961191","weight":"10.0","group_title":"SRG-APP-000277","uuid":"947BD005-6BF8-1014-A94F-99AB03F0CF7A","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000026","rule_id_src":"SV-213450r961191_rule","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","group_id_src":"V-213450","severity":"medium","discussion":"This policy setting allows specifying the day of the week on which to perform a scheduled scan. The scan can also be configured to run every day or to never run at all. This setting can be configured with the following ordinal number values: \n(0x0) Every Day  \n(0x1) Sunday  \n(0x2) Monday  \n(0x3) Tuesday  \n(0x4) Wednesday  \n(0x5) Thursday  \n(0x6) Friday  \n(0x7) Saturday  \n(0x8) Never (default)  \n\nIf this setting is enabled, a scheduled scan will run at the frequency specified. If this setting is disabled or not configured, a scheduled scan will run at a default frequency.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-89917","V-75237"],"mitigations":""},{"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Scan &gt;&gt; \"Turn on e-mail scanning\" is set to \"Enabled\".\n  \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan\n\nCriteria: If the value \"DisableEmailScanning\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000210","id":"V-213451"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Microsoft Defender Antivirus/Scan/Turn on e-mail scanning is set to Enabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:26000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Microsoft Defender Antivirus/Scan/Turn on e-mail scanning is set to Enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:26000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableEmailScanning'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:26000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan'\n                        : name equals 'DisableEmailScanning'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:26","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213451","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Scan &gt;&gt; \"Turn on e-mail scanning\" to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","comments":null,"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to turn on e-mail scanning.","mitigation_control":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","responsibility":"","uuid":"947BD9A3-6BF8-1014-9F2B-8D9516FEB834","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213451r961092","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213451","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89919","V-75239"],"classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting allows the configuration of e-mail scanning. When e-mail scanning is enabled, the engine will parse the mailbox and mail files according to their specific format in order to analyze the mail bodies and attachments. Several e-mail formats are currently supported, for example: pst (Outlook), dbx mbx mime (Outlook Express), binhex (Mac). If this setting is enabled, e-mail scanning will be enabled. If this setting is disabled or not configured, e-mail scanning will be disabled.","rule_id_src":"SV-213451r961092_rule","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000027","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":""},{"weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213452r1190723","uuid":"947BE19B-6BF8-1014-BEE0-D589D1096397","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000276","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000028","rule_id_src":"SV-213452r1190723_rule","discussion":"This policy setting allows defining the number of days that must pass before spyware definitions are considered out of date. If definitions are determined to be out of date, this state may trigger several additional actions, including falling back to an alternative update source or displaying a warning icon in the user interface. By default this value is set to 14 days. \n\nIf this setting is enabled, spyware definitions will be considered out of date after the number of days specified have passed without an update. If this setting is disabled or not configured, spyware definitions will be considered out of date after the default number of days have passed without an update.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-89921","V-75241"],"security_override_guidance":"","severity":"high","group_id_src":"V-213452","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:27"},"group_id":"V-213452","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.1