es\\Define the number of days before spyware definitions are considered out of date_less than 7\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '7'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates'\n                        : name equals 'ASSignatureDue'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '7'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:27001 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before spyware definitions are considered out of date_not 0\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:27000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before spyware definitions are considered out of date\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ASSignatureDue'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:27001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before spyware definitions are considered out of date_not 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates'\n                        : name equals 'ASSignatureDue'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '7'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-213452","title":"SRG-APP-000276"},"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Security Intelligence Updates &gt;&gt; \"Define the number of days before spyware security intelligence considered out of date\" is set to \"Enabled\" and \"7\" or less is selected in the drop-down box (excluding \"0\", which is unacceptable).\n\nIf third-party antispyware is installed and up to date, the Windows Defender AV spyware age requirement will be NA.\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates\n\nCriteria: If the value \"ASSignatureDue\" is REG_DWORD = 7, this is not a finding.\n\nA value of 1 - 6 is also acceptable and not a finding.\n\nA value of 0 is a finding.\n\nA value higher than 7 is a finding.","ccis":["CCI-004964"],"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV spyware definition age must not exceed 7 days.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Signature Updates &gt;&gt; \"Define the number of days before spyware definitions are considered out of date\" to \"Enabled\" and select \"7\" or less in the drop-down box.\n\nDo not select a value of 0. This disables the option.","documentable":"false"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before virus definitions are considered out of date_less than 7)\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before virus definitions are considered out of date_not 0)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:28000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before virus definitions are considered out of date_less than 7\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:28000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before virus definitions are considered out of date\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AVSignatureDue'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:28000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before virus definitions are considered out of date_less than 7\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '7'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates'\n                        : name equals 'AVSignatureDue'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '7'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:28001 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before virus definitions are considered out of date_not 0\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:28000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before virus definitions are considered out of date\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AVSignatureDue'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:28001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Define the number of days before virus definitions are considered out of date_not 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates'\n                        : name equals 'AVSignatureDue'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '7'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_id":"V-213453","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:28"},"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt;Security Intelligence Updates &gt;&gt; \"Define the number of days before virus security intelligence considered out of date\" is set to \"Enabled\" and \"7\" or less is selected in the drop-down box (excluding \"0\", which is unacceptable).\n\nIf third-party antivirus protection is installed and up to date, the Windows Defender Antivirus age requirement is NA.\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates\n\nCriteria: If the value \"AVSignatureDue\" is REG_DWORD = 7, this is not a finding.\n\nA value of 1 - 6 is also acceptable and not a finding.\n\nA value of 0 is a finding.\n\nA value higher than 7 is a finding.","ccis":["CCI-004964"],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000276","id":"V-213453"},"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV virus definition age must not exceed 7 days.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Signature Updates &gt;&gt; \"Define the number of days before virus definitions are considered out of date\" to \"Enabled\" and select \"7\" or less in the drop-down box.\n\nDo not select a value of 0. This disables the option.","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213453r1190724","responsibility":"","uuid":"947BE8F7-6BF8-1014-8B97-A29212EDA434","group_title":"SRG-APP-000276","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213453r1190724_rule","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000029","legacy_ids":["SV-89923","V-75243"],"mitigations":"","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting allows defining the number of days that must pass before virus definitions are considered out of date. If definitions are determined to be out of date, this state may trigger several additional actions, including falling back to an alternative update source or displaying a warning icon in the user interface. By default, this value is set to 14 days. \n\nIf this setting is enabled, virus definitions will be considered out of date after the number of days specified have passed without an update. If this setting is disabled or not configured, virus definitions will be considered out of date after the default number of days have passed without an update.","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"high","group_id_src":"V-213453","security_override_guidance":""},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:29","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213454","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Specify the day of the week to check for definition updates)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:29000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Specify the day of the week to check for definition updates\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:29000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Specify the day of the week to check for definition updates\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ScheduleDay'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:29000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Signature Updates\\Specify the day of the week to check for definition updates\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates'\n                        : name equals 'ScheduleDay'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-213454","title":"SRG-APP-000261"},"ccis":["CCI-001308"],"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Security Intelligence Updates &gt;&gt; \"Specify the day of the week to check for security intelligence updates\" is set to \"Enabled\" and \"Every Day\" is selected in the drop-down box.\n  \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Signature Updates\n\nCriteria: If the value \"ScheduleDay\" is REG_DWORD = 0, this is not a finding.","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to check for definition updates daily.","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Signature Updates &gt;&gt; \"Specify the day of the week to check for definition updates\" to \"Enabled\" and select \"Every Day\" in the drop-down box.","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213454r961161","uuid":"947BF0CF-6BF8-1014-92DD-A7FEBABEB456","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000261","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000030","rule_id_src":"SV-213454r961161_rule","discussion":"This policy setting allows specifying the day of the week on which to check for definition updates. The check can also be configured to run every day or to never run at all. This setting can be configured with the following ordinal number values: \n(0x0) Every Day (default)  \n(0x1) Sunday   \n(0x2) Monday  \n(0x3) Tuesday  \n(0x4) Wednesday  \n(0x5) Thursday  \n(0x6) Friday  \n(0x7) Saturday  \n(0x8) Never  \n\nIf this setting is enabled, the check for definition updates will occur at the frequency specified. If this setting is disabled or not configured, the check for definition updates will occur at a default frequency.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-89925","V-75245"],"mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","group_id_src":"V-213454","severity":"medium"},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:30","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213455","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Threats\\Specify threat alert levels at which default action should not be taken when detected-Severe)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:30000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Threats\\Specify threat alert levels at which default action should not be taken when detected-Severe\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:30000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Threats\\Specify threat alert levels at which default action should not be taken when detected-Severe\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Threats\\ThreatSeverityDefaultAction'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to '5'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:30000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Threats\\Specify threat alert levels at which default action should not be taken when detected-Severe\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Threats\\ThreatSeverityDefaultAction'\n                        : name equals '5'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000207","id":"V-213455"},"ccis":["CCI-001662"],"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Threats &gt;&gt; \"Specify threat alert levels at which default action should not be taken when detected\" is set to \"Enabled\".  \n\nClick the âShowâ¦â box option and verify the \"Value name\" field contains a value of \"5\" and the \"Value\" field  contains \"2\".  A value of \"3\" in the \"Value\" field is more restrictive and also an acceptable value.\n  \nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Threats\\ThreatSeverityDefaultAction\n\nCriteria: If the value \"5\" is REG_SZ = 2 (or 3), this is not a finding.\n","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured for automatic remediation action to be taken for threat alert level Severe.","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Threats &gt;&gt; \"Specify threat alert levels at which default action should not be taken when detected\" to \"Enabled\". \n\nSelect the \"Showâ¦\" option box and enter \"5\" in the \"Value name\" field and enter \"2\" in the \"Value\" field.","status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","rule_id":"SV-213455r961086","weight":"10.0","group_title":"SRG-APP-000207","uuid":"947BF842-6BF8-1014-A1FD-C40C48235059","responsibility":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000031","rule_id_src":"SV-213455r961086_rule","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213455","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"This policy setting allows the customization of which automatic remediation action will be taken for each threat alert level. Threat alert levels should be added under the Options for this setting. Each entry must be listed as a name value pair. The name defines a threat alert level. The value contains the action ID for the remediation action that should be taken. \n\nValid threat alert levels are:  \n1 = Low  \n2 =  Medium  \n4 = High  \n5 = Severe  \n\nValid remediation action values are: \n2 = Quarantine  \n3 = Remove  \n6 = Ignore","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":["SV-89927","V-75247"],"mitigations":""},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","responsibility":"","uuid":"947BFFB7-6BF8-1014-BE34-FF3FA2C637E6","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213456r961092","group_id_src":"V-213456","severity":"medium","security_override_guidance":"","legacy_ids":["SV-92661","V-77965"],"mitigations":"","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","discussion":"This rule blocks the following file types from being run or launched from an email seen in either Microsoft Outlook or webmail (such as Gmail.com or Outlook.com):\nExecutable files (such as .exe, .dll, or .scr)\nScript files (such as a PowerShell .ps, VisualBasic .vbs, or JavaScript .js file)\nScript archive files","rule_id_src":"SV-213456r961092_rule","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000032","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"check_content":"This setting is applicable starting with v1709 of Windows 10. It is NA for prior versions.\n\nVerify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard &gt;&gt; Attack Surface Reduction &gt;&gt; \"Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules\" is set to \"Enabledâ.  Click \"Show...\". Verify the rule ID in the Value name column and the desired state in the Value column is set as follows:\nValue name: BE9BA2D9-53EA-4CDC-84E5-9B1EEEE46550\nValue:  1\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Windows Defender Exploit Guard\\ASR\\Rules\n\nCriteria: If the value \"BE9BA2D9-53EA-4CDC-84E5-9B1EEEE46550\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000210","id":"V-213456"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard\\Attack Surface Reduction\\Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules550)\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND)) (negated)\nTest                    :     true (Verifies the version is v1709 or greater)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:31000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard\\Attack Surface Reduction\\Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules550\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:31000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard\\Attack Surface Reduction\\Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules550\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Windows Defender Exploit Guard\\ASR\\Rules'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'BE9BA2D9-53EA-4CDC-84E5-9B1EEEE46550'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:31000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard\\Attack Surface Reduction\\Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules550\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Windows Defender Exploit Guard\\ASR\\Rules'\n                        : name equals 'BE9BA2D9-53EA-4CDC-84E5-9B1EEEE46550'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997240000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:31001 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies the version is v1709 or greater\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:31001 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Verifies the version is 1709 or greater\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ReleaseId'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:ste:31001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Verifies the version is 1709 or greater\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '1709'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\n                        : name equals 'ReleaseId'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997220000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '2009'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_id":"V-213456","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:31","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Exploit Guard &gt;&gt; Attack Surface Reduction &gt;&gt; \"Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules\" to \"Enabled\". \n\nClick \"Show...\". Set the Value name to \"BE9BA2D9-53EA-4CDC-84E5-9B1EEEE46550\" and the Value to \"1\".","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","comments":null,"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to block executable content from email client and webmail.","mitigation_control":""},{"check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:32","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-213457","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   true (Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard\\Attack Surface Reduction\\Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules)\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND)) (negated)\nTest                    :     true (Verifies the version is v1709 or greater)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:tst:32000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard\\Attack Surface Reduction\\Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:obj:32000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft Defender Antivirus\\Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard\\Attack Surface Reduction\\Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Windows Defender Exploit Guard\\ASR\\Rules'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'n