nt           : Verifies the version is 1709 or greater\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '1709'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\n                        : name equals 'ReleaseId'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997220000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '2009'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000210","id":"V-213457"},"check_content":"This setting is applicable starting with v1709 of Windows 10. It is NA for prior versions.\n\nVerify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard &gt;&gt; Attack Surface Reduction &gt;&gt; \"Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules\" is set to \"Enabledâ.  Click \"Show...\". Verify the rule ID in the Value name column and the desired state in the Value column is set as follows:\nValue name: D4F940AB-401B-4EFC-AADC-AD5F3C50688A\nValue:  1\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Windows Defender Exploit Guard\\ASR\\Rules\n\nCriteria: If the value \"D4F940AB-401B-4EFC-AADC-AD5F3C50688A\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"comments":null,"rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured block Office applications from creating child processes.","mitigation_control":"","third_party_tools":"","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Exploit Guard &gt;&gt; Attack Surface Reduction &gt;&gt; \"Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules\" to \"Enabled\". \n\nClick \"Show...\". Set the Value name to \"D4F940AB-401B-4EFC-AADC-AD5F3C50688A\" and the Value to \"1\".","documentable":"false","status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213457r961092","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","uuid":"947C0761-6BF8-1014-A37D-B56F33F0A292","responsibility":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000033","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213457r961092_rule","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","security_override_guidance":"","group_id_src":"V-213457","severity":"medium","discussion":"Office apps, such as Word or Excel, will not be allowed to create child processes. This is a typical malware behavior, especially for macro-based attacks that attempt to use Office apps to launch or download malicious executables.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-92663","V-77967"]},{"rule_id":"SV-213458r961092","weight":"10.0","responsibility":"","uuid":"947C0EA2-6BF8-1014-81C5-9FA0775BC31F","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213458r961092_rule","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000034","ia_controls":"","legacy_ids":["SV-92665","V-77969"],"mitigations":"","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","discussion":"This rule targets typical behaviors used by suspicious and malicious add-ons and scripts (extensions) that create or launch executable files. This is a typical malware technique. Extensions will be blocked from being used by Office apps. Typically these extensions use the Windows Scripting Host (.wsh files) to run scripts that automate certain tasks or provide user-created add-on features.","group_id_src":"V-213458","severity":"medium