eck = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '1709'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\n                        : name equals 'ReleaseId'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997220000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '2009'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","group_tree":{"id":"V-213460","title":"SRG-APP-000210"},"ccis":["CCI-001170"],"check_content":"This setting is applicable starting with v1709 of Windows 10. It is NA for prior versions.\n\nVerify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard &gt;&gt; Attack Surface Reduction &gt;&gt; \"Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules\" is set to \"Enabled\". Click \"Show...\". Verify the rule ID in the Value name column and the desired state in the Value column is set as follows:\nValue name: D3E037E1-3EB8-44C8-A917-57927947596D \nValue:  1\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Windows Defender Exploit Guard\\ASR\\Rules\n\nCriteria: If the value \"D3E037E1-3EB8-44C8-A917-57927947596D\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000036","rule_id_src":"SV-213460r961092_rule","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","discussion":"JavaScript and VBScript scripts can be used by malware to launch other malicious apps. This rule prevents these scripts from being allowed to launch apps, thus preventing malicious use of the scripts to spread malware and infect machines.","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-92669","V-77973"],"security_override_guidance":"","group_id_src":"V-213460","severity":"medium","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-213460r961092","uuid":"947C26AF-6BF8-1014-AA24-D344DE3BED02","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210"},{"stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000037","rule_id_src":"SV-213461r961092_rule","classification":"Unclassified","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"Malware and other threats can attempt to obfuscate or hide their malicious code in some script files. This rule prevents scripts that appear to be obfuscated from running. It uses the AntiMalwareScanInterface (AMSI) to determine if a script is potentially obfuscated and then blocks such a script or blocks scripts when an attempt is made to access them.","legacy_ids":["SV-92671","V-77975"],"mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-213461","rule_id":"SV-213461r961092","weight":"10.0","uuid":"947C2EA2-6BF8-1014-90E3-87064B6ACED6","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to block execution of potentially obfuscated scripts.","comments":null,"status":"not_a_finding","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Exploit Guard &gt;&gt; Attack Surface Reduction &gt;&gt; \"Configure Attack Surface Reduction rules\" to \"Enabled\". \n\nClick \"Show...\". Set the Value name to \"5BEB7EFE-FD9A-4556-801D-275E5FFC04CC\" and the Value to \"1\".","group_id":"V-213461","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.defenderantivirus:def:36","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antiviru