ws:\nValue name: 92E97FA1-2EDF-4476-BDD6-9DD0B4DDDC7B\nValue:  1\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Windows Defender Exploit Guard\\ASR\\Rules\n\nCriteria: If the value \"92E97FA1-2EDF-4476-BDD6-9DD0B4DDDC7B\" is REG_SZ = 1, this is not a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000210","id":"V-213462"}},{"mitigations":"","legacy_ids":["SV-92675","V-77979"],"discussion":"Enable Microsoft Defender Exploit Guard network protection to prevent employees from using any application to access dangerous domains that may host phishing scams, exploit-hosting sites, and other malicious content on the internet.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","group_id_src":"V-213463","severity":"medium","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","rule_id_src":"SV-213463r961092_rule","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000039","responsibility":"","uuid":"947C395C-6BF8-1014-A8CC-BB33C8C70E2A","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","rule_id":"SV-213463r961092","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","status":"not_a_finding","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Exploit Guard &gt;&gt; Network Protection &gt;&gt; \"Prevent users and apps from accessing dangerous websites\" to \"Enabled\" and select \"Block\" in the drop-down box.","third_party_tools":"","mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must be configured to prevent user and apps from accessing dangerous websites.","comments":null,"ccis":["CCI-001170"],"check_content":"This setting is applicable starting with v1709 of Windows 10, it is NA for prior versions.\n\nVerify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Compone