up_title":"SRG-APP-000210","rule_id":"SV-278658r1190746","weight":"10.0","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"Disabled (Default): If this setting is not configured or disabled, local admins can see exclusions in the Windows Security App or via PowerShell.\n\nEnabled: If this setting is enabled, local admins no longer see the exclusion list in Windows Security App or via PowerShell.O13.\n\nNote: Applying this setting will not remove exclusions, it only prevents them from being visible to local admins. This is reflected in?Get-MpPreference.I13.","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-278658","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000054","rule_id_src":"SV-278658r1190746_rule","group_tree":{"id":"V-278658","title":"SRG-APP-000210"},"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Control whether or not exclusions are visible to Local Admins is set to \"Enabled\"; otherwise, this is a finding.\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\n\nCriteria: If the value \"HideExclusionsFromLocalAdmins\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is \"0\", this is a finding.","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windowsdefav:def:278658"},"group_id":"V-278658","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false ('Control whether or not exclusions are visible to Local Admins' is 'Ena