gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Reporting &gt;&gt; Configure whether to report Dynamic Signature dropped events to \"Enabled\".","status":"open","false_positives":"","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must report Dynamic Signature dropped events.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","uuid":"947CAA43-6BF8-1014-92F9-F3609BE14D53","responsibility":"","rule_id":"SV-278675r1190765","weight":"10.0","security_override_guidance":"","group_id_src":"V-278675","severity":"medium","discussion":"Microsoft Defender Antivirus logs \"Dynamic Signature dropped\" events when it blocks or removes a file based on a dynamically updated signature, but the signature itself is dropped, meaning it was not fully processed or applied. This can indicate a potential issue with signature updates or the system's ability to handle them.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","legacy_ids":[],"mitigations":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000071","rule_id_src":"SV-278675r1190765_rule","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C"},{"mitigation_control":"","rule_title":"Microsoft Defender AV must scan excluded files and directories during quick scans.","comments":null,"status":"open","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Set the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Scan &gt;&gt; Scan excluded files and directories during quick scans to \"Enabled\".","group_id":"V-278676","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windowsdefav:def:278676","href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (QuickScanIncludeExclusions == 1)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan\\QuickScanIncludeExclusions'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:27867600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : QuickScanIncludeExclusions == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:27867600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'QuickScanIncludeExclusions'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan\\QuickScanIncludeExclusions'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000278","id":"V-278676"},"ccis":["CCI-002624"],"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Scan &gt;&gt; Scan excluded files and directories during quick scans is set to \"Enabled\"; otherwise, this is a finding.\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Scan\n\nCriteria: If the value \"QuickScanIncludeExclusions\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 0, this is a finding.","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","potential_impacts":"","ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000072","rule_id_src":"SV-278676r1190767_rule","discussion":"In Microsoft Defender Antivirus, when an exclusion for a file or folder is created, it will generally be skipped during both real-time protection and on-demand scans (including quick scans and full scans). However, with newer releases, the option exists to configure quick scans to include files and directories that are otherwise excluded from real-time protection.","reference_identifier":"3985","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"security_override_guidance":"","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-278676","rule_id":"SV-278676r1190767","weight":"10.0","uuid":"947CB0F6-6BF8-1014-8E22-EB7C5DCEB653","responsibility":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278"},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000210","uuid":"947CB64A-6BF8-1014-B65B-DCCE560FCF64","responsibility":"","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-278677r1190769","security_override_guidance":"","group_id_src":"V-278677","severity":"medium","reference_identifier":"3985","discussion":"If a site URL has an unknown or uncertain reputation, a toast notification presents the user with the following options:\n\n- Ok: The toast notification is released (removed), and the attempt to access the site is ended.\n\n- Unblock: The user has access to the site for 24 hours, at which point the block is reenabled. The user can continue to use Unblock to access the site until such time that the administrator prohibits (blocks) the site, thus removing the option to Unblock.\n\n- Feedback: The toast notification presents the user with a link to submit a ticket, which the user can use to submit feedback to the administrator in an attempt to justify access to the site.","classification":"Unclassified","mitigations":"","legacy_ids":[],"ia_controls":"","rule_version":"WNDF-AV-000074","rule_id_src":"SV-278677r1190769_rule","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"94765B2D-6BF8-1014-890D-C12B2755253C","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000210","id":"V-278677"},"check_content":"Verify the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Defender Antivirus &gt;&gt; Network Inspection System &gt;&gt; Convert warn verdict to block is set to \"Enabled\"; otherwise, this is a finding.\n\nProcedure: Use the Windows Registry Editor to navigate to the following key: \nHKLM\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\NIS\n\nCriteria: If the value \"EnableConvertWarnToBlock\" is REG_DWORD = 1, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the value is 0, this is a finding.","ccis":["CCI-001170"],"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Defender_Antivirus_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV14-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windowsdefav:def:278677"},"group_id":"V-278677","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:22\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (EnableConvertWarnToBlock == 1)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\NIS\\EnableConvertWarnToBlock'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:27867700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : EnableConvertWarnToBlock == 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must 